ory barriers | 1 | Stable | Certifications exist but not exclusive |\n| Data moat | 1 | Widening | Digital/software in imaging & monitoring |\n| **Total** | **9/21** | **Stable-to-Widening** | **Narrow moat** |\n\n**Step 2-3 \u2014 Lynch classification**\n**Stalwart-to-Fast-Grower hybrid.** Revenue CAGR 3.9% (5-yr) [Arithmetic]; EPS CAGR ~8-10% driven by margin expansion and buybacks. Key checkpoints: (a) inventory +11% in FY25 vs revenue +4% [Arithmetic] \u2014 flag for demand-vs-stock mismatch; (b) book-to-bill 1.06 (Q2-26) [Actual] \u2014 positive forward signal; (c) PEG ~1.9 on adjusted EPS growth vs vendor PEG 1.74 \u2014 not cheap.\n\n**Step 2-4 \u2014 Financial strength scorecard**\n\n| Metric | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue growth (5-yr CAGR / TTM) | +3.9% / +4.0% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Operating margin (TTM / 12-yr median) | 17.0% / 14.8% | [Arithmetic] |\n| ROE (GAAP) / Adjusted ROE | 14.9% / ~19-20% | [Actual vendor] / [Estimate] |\n| ROIC (GAAP) / Tangible adjusted | ~12% / ~30% | [Estimate] / [Estimate] |\n| FCF margin (FY25) / OCF/NI | 13.8% / 1.23x | [Arithmetic] |\n| Net debt/EBITDA | $1.908B / $1.96B \u2248 1.0x | [Estimate] |\n| Interest coverage (FY25) | $1.373B / ~$0.116B \u2248 11.8x | [Arithmetic] |\n| Cash | $1.677B | [Filed] |\n\n**Judgment: Excellent.**\n\n**Step 2-5 \u2014 Capital allocation scorecard (15 pts)**\n\n| Criterion | Score | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 2/3 | Share count \u221218.8% since 2014 (\u22121.5%/yr) [Arithmetic]; but some repurchases at >20x P/E |\n| M&A track record | 3/3 | Six cryogenic bolt-ons over 3 years; De-Sta-Co sale + minority gain \u2248 $1.3B realized [Actual, Q4-24 PR] |\n| Capex efficiency | 3/3 | Capex 2.7% of revenue [Arithmetic] yet 3.9% rev CAGR; incremental margin 38% (Q2-26) [Actual] |\n| Rationality of mix | 3/3 | \"Balance sheet remains a competitive advantage\" [Actual]; balanced toolkit |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3/3 | FY26 guidance raised at Q2 (10.45-10.65 \u2192 10.55-10.75) [Actual] |\n| **Total** | **14/15** | **Excellent** |\n\nInsider: ownership 1.26% [Actual vendor]; no cluster buys; no adjustment.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2.5-1 \u2014 R&D capitalization:** Not separately disclosed; engineering embedded in SG&A/COGS [Unconfirmed] \u2192 no adjustment. Model confidence unaffected (R&D not a decision-driver at DOV).\n\n**Step 2.5-2 \u2014 SBC treatment:** SBC = $0.044B (FY25) [Filed] = 0.5% of revenue, 3.7% of FCF. Adjusted TTM FCF = $1.177B \u2212 $0.044B = **$1.133B [Arithmetic]**. All forward FCF models in \u00a73 subtract SBC.\n\n**Step 2.5-3 \u2014 Operating leases:** $0.247B (FY25) [Filed] added to debt in net-debt figure (see \u00a73). No further capitalization needed.\n\n**Step 2.5-4 \u2014 Brand/data assets:** Not material for a diversified industrial; excludes consumer-brand premium.\n\n**Step 2.5-5 \u2014 Adjusted ROIC:** Adjusted EBIT (FY26E) \u2248 $1.91B [Estimate]; NOPAT \u2248 $1.53B (tax 19.7%). Tangible invested capital = Equity $7.405B \u2212 estimated goodwill/intangibles ~$4.5B [Unconfirmed] + net debt $1.908B \u2248 $4.8B [Estimate]. **Adjusted tangible ROIC \u2248 32% [Estimate]** vs GAAP ROIC ~12% [Estimate]. Gap of ~20pp explained by decades of acquired goodwill \u2014 the economic engine is high-quality, but the GAAP balance sheet hides it.\n\n**Step 2.5-6 \u2014 Owner earnings (FY25):** NI $1.094B + D&A $0.380B \u2212 maintenance capex ~$0.176B (80% of capex) \u2212 \u0394WC $0.300B (FY25 use) = **$0.998B [Estimate]**. Normalized (no WC swing): ~$1.3B.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**3-1. Net debt (my component selection \u2014 declared)**\nDebt = LT $2.621B + current portion/ST borrowings $0.707B + finance leases $0.010B + operating leases $0.247B = **$3.585B [Filed components; sum is my judgment]**.\nCross-check: vendor total-debt scalar $3.575B [Aggregator] \u2014 agreement within 0.3%, so I do not suspect double-counting for this name. Cash $1.677B [Filed]. **Net debt = $1.908B [Estimate]**. EV = $27.274B + $1.908B = **$29.18B**.\n\n**3-2. Forecast \u2014 Explicit base case (all FCF figures after SBC deduction)**\n\n| Line | FY25A | FY26E | FY27E | FY28E | FY29E | FY30E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Revenue ($B) | 8.093 | 8.577 | 9.006 | 9.456 | 9.929 | 10.426 |\n| Revenue growth | +4.5% | +6.0% | +5.0% | +5.0% | +5.0% | +5.0% |\n| EBIT margin (GAAP) | 17.0% | 19.2%* | 19.4%* | 19.6%* | 19.8%* | 20.0%* |\n| EBIT ($B) | 1.373 | 1.647 | 1.747 | 1.853 | 1.966 | 2.085 |\n| NOPAT @19.7% tax | 1.102 | 1.322 | 1.402 | 1.488 | 1.578 | 1.674 |\n| D&A ($B) | 0.380 | 0.395 | 0.432 | 0.454 | 0.477 | 0.500 |\n| Capex ($B) | 0.220 | 0.232 | 0.243 | 0.255 | 0.268 | 0.282 |\n| \u0394WC ($B) | \u22120.300 | \u22120.150 | \u22120.044 | \u22120.046 | \u22120.048 | \u22120.050 |\n| SBC ($B) | 0.044 | 0.045 | 0.045 | 0.045 | 0.045 | 0.045 |\n| **FCFF ($B)** | **1.118A** | **1.290** | **1.502** | **1.596** | **1.694** | **1.797** |\n| FCF margin | 13.8% | 15.0% | 16.7%* | 16.9%* | 17.1%* | 17.2%* |\n\n\\* Implied bridge. The FY26 anchor is **management FCF guidance of 14\u201316% of revenue; midpoint 15.0% \u2192 FCFF $1.287B** [Actual guidance; $1.290B in table rounds to the same]. The EBIT margin row is *derived* from the FCF path \u2014 it is not a separate input; it reconciles to adjusted EPS guidance of $10.55\u201310.75 [Actual] when ~200-300bp of restructuring/purchase-accounting add-backs are included (Q2-26 adjusted-to-GAAP delta is visible in the PR: adj. EPS $2.74 vs GAAP $2.31 [Actual, PR reconciliation]).\nRevenue growth source: FY26 = company guidance midpoint 6\u20138% [Actual]. FY27-30 = **5.0%/yr [Assumption]** \u2014 4% organic (Q2-26 organic growth was 5% [Actual]; guide 4\u20136% [Actual]) + ~1% M&A (Cloeren closed Aug-2026 [Actual]; pipeline \"robust\" [Actual \u2014 mgmt commentary]).\nFCF margin source: FY26 = company guidance midpoint 15% [Actual]. FY27-30 = 16.7\u201317.2% [Assumption] \u2014 requires +170-220bp from guided level; supported by 38% incremental margins [Actual] and the mix shift toward 25% secular-growth platforms [Actual], but this is the single most optimistic input in the base case and sits ABOVE the 14\u201316% guided band. I label this deliberately: *the base case already assumes the company beats its own FCF guidance permanently from 2027 onward.*\nD&A: FY26 [Assumption] from FY25 $0.380B + growth;