he Base to **$162** \u2014 i.e., assume FY27-30 FCF margins of 15.4/15.8/16.2/16.5% instead of 16.7/16.9/17.1/17.2%. That is the $162 case already tabulated in the scenario section. The higher bridge shows the upside sensitivity; the shaded case is my point estimate, because I refuse to build a base case that permanently beats the guided FCF band without line-item evidence of the release (which the pack cannot supply \u2014 Q&A not held [Unconfirmed]).\n\n**Final Base IV = $162 [Estimate]**; the unambiguous range across my defensible inputs (WACC 8.5-10%, g 2.5-3.5%) is **$137-205**, with the market price at $201.92 sitting at the top of that range.\n\n**3-5. Reverse DCF (what the market is pricing)**\nAt $201.92, EV $29.18B, my explicit FCF path: implied required WACC \u2248 **8.0\u20138.3%** (if terminal g=3%), or implied 2030 FCF margin \u2248 **21.5%** (if WACC=9.3%) \u2014 far above company guidance. Equivalently the market is paying 19.0x forward adjusted EPS for ~10% growth \u2014 i.e., pricing ~5 years of flawless execution with no discount for the cyclical segments. **Feasible, but at the upper boundary; not excessive only if the FCF-margin bull case is realized.**\n\n**3-6. Multiples cross-check**\n\n| Metric | DOV | Comment |\n|---|---|---|\n| Trailing P/E | 24.0x [Arithmetic] | vs 12-yr median ~20x [Estimate] |\n| Fwd adjust. P/E | 18.9x | Peers ITW ~22-24x, ROP ~28-32x, PH ~24x [Estimate] \u2014 DOV discount justified by 4-5% organic growth |\n| P/FCF TTM | 24.1x (on adj. FCF $1.133B) | Rich |\n| EV/EBITDA TTM GAAP | 16.6x [Arithmetic] | Above own 12-yr median ~13x [Estimate] |\n| EV/EBITDA FY26E adj. | 13.3x | Reasonable |\n| P/B | 3.69x on 14.9% ROE | Justified P/B at 9.3% CoE \u2248 2.0-2.2x [Computed]; market implies ROE improvement to ~20%+ |\n\n**Multiples cross-check: valuation is fair on forward EV/EBITDA but rich on FCF, P/B, and trailing P/E.** Not a DCF-only conclusion \u2014 three independent lenses (DCF, multiples, reverse DCF) all cluster around \"at-or-above fair value.\"\n\n**3-7. Tornado sensitivity \u2014 Top 3 variables (become Thesis KPIs)**\n\n| Variable | -1\u03c3 / Low | Base | +1\u03c3 / High | IV swing |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **WACC (8.0\u201310.0%)** | $144 | $162 | ~$208 | \u00b127% |\n| **FCF margin by 2030 (14\u201318%)** | $137 | $162 | ~$176 | \u00b114% |\n| **Terminal g (2.5\u20133.5%)** | $152 | $162 | ~$174 | \u00b17% |\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Competitive response (\u22122):** Success in polymer processing (Cloeren), cryogenics, and single-use biopharma invites ITW, IDEX, Graco, Emerson to raise bids in future M&A. The \"improved M&A market\" comment [Actual] signals a seller's market \u2014 overpayment risk rises.\n**Reflexivity (+2):** Strong equity currency, A-credit, \"competitive advantage\" balance sheet [Actual] attract talent and deal flow; high multiple feeds acquisitions. The negative loop (de-rating \u2192 M&A currency weakens, SBC attractiveness drops) is real but starts only below ~$170.\n**Customer behavior (+2):** Aftermarket/consumables grow with installed base; biopharma single-use components are sticky once validated. As penetration grows, LTV/CAC improves for secular platforms.\n**Net: +2 \u2014 modest positive, already embedded in the FCF-margin path.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nPrior (base rates): double-digit EPS growth 5-yr ~40%; mid-single-digit ~35%; cyclical disappointment ~25%.\nUpdate evidence: Q2-26 bookings +16%, book-to-bill 1.06, guidance raised [Actual] \u2192 posterior = **Base 55%, Bull 25%, Bear 20%**.\n\n| Scenario (prob.) | Rev path | FCF margin path | WACC / g | IV |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Base (55%)** | FY26 8.577 [+6%]; FY27-30 +5.0%/yr | 15.0% \u2192 16.5% | 9.3% / 3.0% | **$162** |\n| **Bull (25%)** | FY26 8.656 [+7%]; FY27-30 +6.0%/yr | 15.5% \u2192 18.0% | 9.0% / 3.5% | **$205** |\n| **Bear (20%)** | FY26 8.45 [+4%]; FY27-30 +2.0%/yr (recession) | 13.5% \u2192 11.5% \u2192 12.0% | 10.0% / 2.5% | **$83** |\n\n**Expected IV = 0.55\u00d7162 + 0.25\u00d7205 + 0.20\u00d783 = $157 [Estimate]**\n**50% CI: ~$130\u2013190; 80% CI: ~$90\u2013235 [Estimate]**\n**MoS = (157 \u2212 201.92)/157 = \u221228.6% \u2192 None.**\n(Base-case MoS vs $162 = \u221224.6%. At T0 there is **no margin of safety** under any of my scenarios; the price is only justified by the full bull path.)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u