7 (38% incremental margins [Actual], $40M rightsizing savings [Estimate, research brief])\n- Cloeren and 2026-27 bolt-ons deliver >WACC ROIC within 3 years\n- Clean Energy + Climate book-to-bill stays >1.0 for four more quarters\n- Fed cuts \u2192 market-implied WACC falls toward 8%; price re-rates to $220-240\n- 2026 adjusted EPS hits $10.75 (top of raised guide) \u2192 forward P/E compresses to 18.8x\n\n**Downside risks:**\n- 2027-28 US recession \u2192 Climate/can-making collapse, bookings \u221220%, FCF margin to 11-12% \u2192 my Bear $83\n- PFAS/compliance costs: research brief cites $235.3M [Unconfirmed \u2014 not verified from filings]; litigation overhang caps multiple\n- Margin expansion stalls: input inflation, tariffs (listed risk factor in Q2-26 PR [Actual]), SG&A growth\n- M&A overpayment in an \"improved\" seller's market; Cloeren integration failure\n- Inventory build (+11% FY25 vs +4% revenue [Arithmetic]) unwinds negatively if demand slows\n- FX headwinds on 45.6% non-US revenue [Estimate]\n\n**Pre-mortem (2026\u21922031 failure scenarios):**\n1. *Recession + cyclical segments* \u2192 FCF margin 10-12%, price $120-140. Early-warning: book-to-bill <0.9 for two quarters; FCF margin <13%; Climate segment revenue declining >10% for 3 quarters.\n2. *M&A discipline breaks* \u2192 deals >$2B aggregate, ROIC < WACC by 2029. Early-warning: deal size disclosure, rising goodwill, segment R&D cuts.\n3. *Regulatory/PFAS overhang* \u2192 damages >$500M, \"quality\" brand impaired. Early-warning: litigation disclosures in 10-Q, payout ratios rising >30% of adjusted EPS (current 18.8% [Arithmetic]).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **Common bear triggers:** US recession (sensitivity +2), industrial capex downturn, dollar spike (45.6% non-US revenue), 10Y >5% (high-for-longer).\n- **Tail correlation:** If the portfolio holds ITW/PH/ROP/Graco/EMR, DOV offers near-zero diversification in a 2008/2020/2022-style stress \u2014 all names de-rate together. Treat the weighted exposure to multi-industrials as one bet.\n- **CVaR (5% tail):** At beta ~1.15 (vendor), a severe industrial drawdown (\u221240% sector) implies DOV \u221235-45% \u2192 price $110-130; my bear case ($83) covers the extreme 5% tail.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM (Short thesis, using the same data)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n1. **Valuation has no cushion:** 24x trailing GAAP P/E, 24x TTM FCF, 3.7x P/B \u2014 versus 12-yr medians of ~20x / ~18x / ~3.0x [Arithmetic/Estimate]. The stock is priced for the 17%+ FCF-margin path that the company itself has never guided.\n2. **FCF conversion is cyclical, not structurally strong:** FY22 FCF margin 6.2%, FY24 11.9%, FY25 13.8% [Arithmetic]. The 14-16% FY26 guide is at a cyclical high-water mark, not the through-cycle norm.\n3. **Climate & Sustainability segment declined \u221211.2% in 2025** [Estimate \u2014 research brief citing qz.com]; can-making equipment is late-cycle; the largest end-market is still heavy in project timing.\n4. **Inventory build (+11% vs +4% revenue, FY25 [Arithmetic])** usually ends with a production cut and a WC drag \u2014 my model already assumes a WC headwind, but equity analysts may not.\n5. **PFAS/regulatory exposure of $235.3M** [Unconfirmed \u2014 research brief] plus \"production-related issues\" as top risk factor [Estimate, research brief] \u2014 a quiet cost overhang in a \"clean\" quality narrative.\n6. **95.2% institutional ownership** [Aggregator] \u2014 ETF redemption loops amplify downside; no natural under-owned buyer.\n7. **Late-cycle M&A tells:** \"M&A markets have improved this year,\" \"pipeline has a number of opportunities,\" \"balance sheet remains a competitive advantage\" [Actual \u2014 management, Q2-26 call] \u2014 this is the exact language that precedes overpayment at cycles' highs.\n\n**Logic combat:** Long strongest = (a) ~30% tangible ROIC, (b) +520bp OI-margin expansion over 9 years, (c) 14/15 capital-allocation score. Short strongest = (a) zero MoS, (b) cyclical FCF conversion, (c) inventory + late-cycle M&A signals. **Score: Long 6/10, Short 7/10 \u2014 gap = 1, below the 2-point threshold**: long conviction is downgraded one step; no \"Buy.\"\n\n**Killed arguments (and revival conditions):**\n- *\"Dover is a conglomerate discount story\"* \u2014 killed by 9 years of consistent margin expansion and portfolio reshaping; would revive if OI margin <15% for two consecutive years.\n- *\"SBC is a shareholder cost\"* \u2014 killed by data: 0.5% of revenue [Filed]; would revive if SBC >1.5% of revenue.\n- *\"The 2024 earnings spike proves unsustainable EPS\"* \u2014 killed: FY24 NI $2.697B was driven by disclosed one-time gains (De-Sta-Co + minority investment) [Actual, Q4-24 PR]; continuing-ops earnings were $1.4B, adjusted $1.15B; the 2025-26 normal level is $1.1-1.4B.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n| KPI | Threshold (thesis intact) | Re-evaluate if |\n|---|---|---|\n| FCF margin (quarterly, annualized) | 14\u201316% (guided); 16%+ would lift IV toward $175+ | <13% for 2 quarters |\n| Book-to-bill | \u22651.0 | <0.9 for 2 quarters \u2192 Bear trigger |\n| Adjusted EPS (FY26) | $10.55\u201310.75 | Miss <$10.30 with organic growth <4% |\n| Organic growth | 4\u20136% | <2% for 2 quarters |\n| Climate segment | Stabilize in H2-26 | Continued >10% decline for 4 quarters |\n| M&A | <$1.5B/yr, bolt-on only | Deal >$2B, or goodwill step-up >20% |\n| PFAS/litigation | No new material accrual | New accrual >$100M \u2192 shrink IV by up to 15% |\n| Inventory/revenue spread | \u22644pp | >8pp for 2 quarters |\n\nCheck cadence: quarterly within 10 days of the 10-Q; full pre-mortem refresh every 6 months (conviction decay 