 0 | n/a |\n| Cost advantage | 2 | Stable |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening |\n| Regulatory barriers | 1 | Stable |\n| Data moat | 1 | Widening |\n| **Total** | **10** | **Narrow moat, stable-to-widening** |\n\n**Step 2-3 Lynch class**\n\n**Stalwart / Cyclical hybrid.** Low cyclicality due to aftermarket and consumable mix; 5-yr revenue CAGR 3.9%, but order momentum points to recovery in 2026\u201327. Key Lynch check: margin expansion plus modest growth is the value path; DOV is executing that path \u2014 Q2 2026 incremental margin 38%, +80bps EBITDA margin to 25.9% [Actual].\n\n**Step 2-4 Financial strength scorecard**\n\n- Revenue growth 3-yr CAGR: ~+1.8% [Arithmetic \u2014 2022\u201325]\n- 4Q rolling revenue growth: +6.9% YoY [Actual]\n- GAAP operating margin: FY2025 17.0%; TTM 17.0% [Actual]\n- Adjusted EBITDA margin: 25.9% [Actual \u2014 Q2 2026]\n- ROE: 14.9% [Aggregator]\n- FCF conversion: FY2025 OCF $1.338B less capex $0.220B vs NI $1.094B = **102%** [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt/EBITDA: ~1.1x [Estimate \u2014 adjusted EBITDA]\n- Interest coverage: >12x [Estimate]\n- Balance sheet: strong; net debt $1.9B vs market cap $27.3B\n\n**Judgment: Good-to-Excellent.**\n\n**Step 2-5 Capital allocation scorecard**\n\n| Item | Score (0\u20133) |\n|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 2 \u2014 net buybacks most years, but pace modest; 2026 $1B program announced [Actual] |\n| M&A track record | 2 \u2014 $2B ESG divestiture + $700M 2025 acquisitions; history improves over 3yrs [Estimate] |\n| Capex efficiency | 2 \u2014 capex only 2.7% of sales; incremental margins 38% show good capital efficiency [Actual] |\n| Rationality of mix | 2 \u2014 balanced buyback/dividend/M&A/disciplined capex |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3 \u2014 Q2 2026 beat, full-year guidance raised [Actual] |\n| **Total** | **11 / 15** |\n\nNo insider ownership bonus/penalty: insider ownership 1.26%, no 6-month cluster reported [Unconfirmed].\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\n- **SBC adjustment [Actual]:** FY2025 SBC $44M. Adjusted FCF = OCF $1.338B \u2212 capex $0.220B \u2212 SBC $0.044B = **$1.074B**.\n- **R&D capitalization [Assumption]:** DOV appears to report modest R&D; I do not reclassify it, as R&D is proportionally small versus OI.\n- **Operating leases [Actual]:** FY2025 operating lease liability $0.247B added to debt.\n- **Owner earnings FY2025 [Estimate]:** NI $1.094B + D&A $0.380B \u2212 total capex $0.220B \u2212 working-capital rebuild (ex-cash) \u2248 **$1.10\u2013$1.25B**. \n- **Adjusted ROIC [Estimate]:** NOPAT \u2248 $1.10B on invested capital \u2248 $9.0\u2013$9.5B \u2192 ROIC \u2248 **12\u201312.5%**, comfortably above WACC.\n- **GAAP ROIC** \u2248 10\u201311%; gap <5pp, caused by modest R&D and SBC treatment only.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\n**Step 0-1/0-2/0-3/0-4 \u2014 Engine selection.** DOV is a **Quality Compounder** within a cyclical industrial envelope. I use **Engine 1** as the lead engine. I reject Engine 2 as lead because 12-year revenue history shows modest cyclical amplitude; I reject Engine 4/5 because growth is not option-led or binary. Transition status: not in transition.\n\n**Discount rate derivation**\n\n| Input | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Risk-free rate | 4.71% | [Actual \u2014 10Y UST 2026-08-21] |\n| Equity beta | 1.16 | [Aggregator \u2014 window not stated] |\n| ERP | 4.5% | [Assumption \u2014 broad institutional range] |\n| Cost of equity | 4.71 + 1.16\u00d74.5 = 9.91% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Pre-tax cost of debt | ~3.3% | [Estimate \u2014 FY2026 H1 interest expense annualized ~$117M on debt $3.585B] |\n| After-tax cost of debt | 3.3% \u00d7 (1\u22120.20) = 2.64% | [Estimate] |\n| Equity weight / Debt weight | 88.4% / 11.6% | [Arithmetic] |\n| **WACC** | **9.0%** | [Assumption \u2014 rounded from ~9.1%] |\n\n**Forecast drivers**\n\n- 2026 revenue: $8.66B \u2014 guidance 6\u20138% total growth [Actual]\n- 2027 revenue: $9.09B \u2014 consensus +5.1% [Estimate]\n- 2028\u201330 revenue: +4%/yr [Assumption \u2014 below the guided year, not established; I show explicit range in the sensitivity table]\n- GAAP operating margin: 17.5% (2026) \u2192 18.8% (2030) [Assumption \u2014 based on Q2 2026 GAAP op margin 17.9%, 38% incremental margin, and adjusted EBITDA margin 25.9%]\n- Tax rate: 20% [Estimate \u2014 H1 2026 effective tax rate 19.7%]\n- D&A: rises from $0.420B to $0.490B [Estimate]\n- Capex: 2.8% of revenue [Estimate \u2014 2025 actual 2.7%]\n- Working-capital drag: 0.3% of revenue [Assumption]\n- Terminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 below long-run nominal GDP]\n\n**Explicit DCF forecast ($B)**\n\n| FY | Revenue | OI margin | NOPAT | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | FCFF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 8.66 | 17.5% | 1.213 | 0.420 | 0.242 | 0.026 | 1.365 |\n| 2027 | 9.09 | 17.9% | 1.302 | 0.430 | 0.255 | 0.027 | 1.450 |\n| 2028 | 9.45 | 18.2% | 1.376 | 0.450 | 0.265 | 0.028 | 1.533 |\n| 2029 | 9.83 | 18.5% | 1.455 | 0.470 | 0.275 | 0.029 | 1.621 |\n| 2030 | 10.22 | 18.8% | 1.537 | 0.490 | 0.286 | 0.031 | 1.710 |\n\nTerminal FCFF = $1.710B \u00d7 1.03 = $1.761B\nTerminal value = $1.761B / (0.09 \u2212 0.03) = $30.24B\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| PV FY2026\u201330 FCFF | $5.916B |\n| PV terminal value | $19.66B |\n| Enterprise value | $25.58B |\n| + cash \u2212 total debt | $25.58 + $1.677 \u2212 $3.585 = $23.67B |\n| Equity value per share | $23.67B / 135.073M = **$175.20** |\n\n**DCF sensitivity \u2014 per share**\n\n| WACC | TV g = 2.5% | g = 3.0% | g = 3.5% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8.5% | $181 | $192 | $206 |\n| 9.0% | $160 | $175 | $189 |\n| 9.5% | $145 | $160 | $174 |\n\n**Reverse DCF:** Current price $201.92 implies either a terminal exit at ~19x EV/EBITDA (too rich for a narrow-moat industrial), or WACC <8.5% with 3.5% terminal growth, or 2030 operating margins >20%. These are possible but are the **top of the plausible range**, not the base case.\n\n**Multiple cross-check**\n\n- 2026 adjusted EPS guidance $10.55\u2013$10.75 [Actual]; at 18\u201320x \u2192 $190\u2013$215.\n- 2027 consensus EPS $11.64 [Estimate]; at 17\u201319x \u2192 $198\u2013$221.\n- Peer forward multiple: Parker-Hannifin ~28.5x [Aggregator]. DOV deserves a discount due to lower growth/ROIC; 18\u201319x forward is fair for quality.\n- Current forward P/E on 2027 consensus: $201.92 / $11.64 = **17.3x** \u2014 moderately below fair if consensus is right.\n\n**Blended IV**\n\nDCF at 60%, earnings multiple at 40%:\n(0.60 \u00d7 $175) + (0.40 \u00d7 $209) = **$188.60** \u2192 **Base intrinsic value \u2248 $190**.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n- **Competitive response:** If DOV\u2019s secular-growth segments (AI/data-center, clean energy, sustainability) continue to compound, ITW, Fortive, and Emerson will likely step up M&A into adjacent niches \u2014 modest long-term margin pressure, but DOV\u2019s niche focus limits direct price wars. Net: \u22120.5 to the model.\n- **Reflexivity:** Positive feedback already visible: strong stock price \u2192 cheap SBC \u2192 equity M&A currency; Q2 2026 management notes M&A markets have improved and acquisition pipeline is attractive [Actual].\n- **Customer behavior:** Book-to-bill = 1.06 [Actual] shows early-cyclical order conversion. As penetration grows in sustainability and clean-energy fueling, LTV should rise with recurring software/consumables attach. No evidence yet of churn or LTV degradation [Unconfirmed].\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE\n\n**Step 4-1/4-2 Scenarios and probabilities**\n\n| Scenario | Prob | Description | Per-share value |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 20% | Industrial recession in 2027; revenue \u22128%; operating margin compresses to 15%; WACC rises to 9.5% | $140 |\n| Base | 55% | Guided 2026, 5% 2027, 4% thereafter; margins to 18.8% by 2030 | $190 |\n| Bull | 25% | Secular-growth revenue exceeds 30% of portfolio; margin reaches 20%; M&A accretive; multiple expands to 21x | $235 |\n\n**Step 4-3 Bayesian update**\n\nPrior (from base rates): Recession/stall 25%, Base 50%, Upside 25%.\nPosterior (after 3 consecutive quarters of double-digit bookings, FY26 guidance raise, book-to-bill >1.0): **Bear 20%, Base 55%, Bull 25%.**\n\n**Step 4-4/4-5 Expected price and margin of safety**\n\nExpected value = 0.20\u00d7$140 + 0.55\u00d7$190 + 0.25\u00d7$235 = **$191.25**\nMoS = ($191.25 \u2212 $201.92) / $191.25 = **\u22125.6%**\n\n- 50% CI: **$170\u2013$215**\n- 80% CI: **$140\u2013$260**\n\nThe stock is **slightly overvalued** relative to base intrinsic value; the risk/reward is asymmetric to the downside at T0.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 4.5. HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nCurrent price embeds roughly **6\u20137 years** of 5%+ earnings growth at the consensus margin path. My natural horizon is 3\u20135 years. The spread is only ~1\u20132 years, not >2 years, so no meaningful horizon-arbitrage opportunity exists. Avoid treating DOV as a deep-value multi-year catch-up trade.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\n**Conviction score (0\u201315)**\n\n| Criterion | Score |\n|---|---|\n| Business quality | 3 |\n| Valuation attractiveness | 1 |\n| Macro alignment | 2 |\n| Thesis clarity | 2 |\n| Execution traceability | 3 |\n| **Total** | **11 / 15** \u2192 **High conviction on business, low conviction on entry** |\n\nApplying conviction decay: \u22121 point if no confirming evidence within 6 months \u2192 **10/15**.\n\n**Sizing:** Max position weight at 11/15 conviction is **8%**; reduce by 1pp for +1.1 beta and 1pp for 15% recession probability; reduce 2pp for negative MoS. **Target maximum: 4\u20135%.** No new money at T0.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- Short % of float: 2.84%, shares short 3.32M, days-to-cover 2.9, MoM change \u22128.9% [Aggregator \u2014 stale]. No squeeze setup.\n- Institutional ownership: 95.19% [Aggregator]. High passive/active overlap; ETF flow could distort short-term price.\n- Insider ownership: 1.26%; no insider cluster signal [Unconfirmed].\n- Options positioning: not held [Unconfirmed].\n- Sentiment: analyst mean target $246.89 with 13 strong-buy/4 hold/1 sell [Aggregator]. Mildly positive, not extreme.\n- **Crowding risk: 6/15** \u2014 moderate, no position-size penalty applied separately beyond beta/recession adjustments.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nDOV offers:\n- Diversified industrial exposure with **low commodity beta** relative to pure energy/materials.\n- **Hedging value** vs a tech-heavy portfolio.\n- **Interest-rate sensitivity** \u2014 10Y at 4.7% is a headwind, so DOV overlaps with a value/industrial barbell.\n\nNo single bear trigger dominates; the common portfolio risks are (1) global industrial recession and (2) rates >5.5%. Beta 1.16 raises portfolio CVaR modestly.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\n- Expected return vs T0: ($191.25 + dividend ~$2.00 \u2212 $201.92)/$201.92 = **\u22124.3%** over 12 months, ignoring volatility.\n- Edge is negative \u2192 full Kelly \u2264 0. Fractional Kelly (0.25\u00d7) = **0%**.\n- For existing holders, Kelly-derived trim target is the level I would arrive at **if treating valuation alone**; I do not force a sale because quality/execution score is high, but I do not add.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\n**Risks**\n\n1. **Multiple compression** \u2014 current P/E 25.5x trailing, 18.9x forward adjusted; if 10Y rises above 5.25%, fair forward multiple could drop to 16x \u2192 $186 on 2027 EPS.\n2. **Cyclical drawdown** \u2014 12-year data shows revenue fell 20% from 2014 to 2016; a repeat would cut FY2027 revenue to ~$7.8B and EPS below $9.\n3. **M&A integration** \u2014 $700M spent in 2025; Cloeren acquisition 2026; large deals historically destroy value ~30% of the time.\n4. **PFAS/environmental liability** \u2014 web brief cites $235.3M PFAS compliance/litigation exposure; I could not verify from filings [Unconfirmed]. Included in bear scenario as a $3\u20134/share hit.\n5. **FX** \u2014 weak dollar helps now; reversal would pressure EPS 2\u20133%.\n6. **Capacity constraints** \u2014 lead times lengthening; lost sales risk if capacity expansion lags orders.\n\n**Catalysts**\n\n- Full-year 2026 guidance raised: GAAP EPS $8.94\u2013$9.14, adjusted EPS $10.55\u2013$10.75 [Actual].\n- Bookings +16% YoY, book-to-bill 1.06 [Actual] \u2192 2H26 revenue visibility.\n- Secular-growth markets = ~25% of portfolio [Actual], targeted to be a larger share.\n- $1B buyback authorization [Actual].\n- Rightsizing savings of ~$40M [Estimate \u2014 web brief].\n- Cloeren acquisition expands polymer-processing extrusion niche [Actual \u2014 Dover press release].\n- Potential M&A pipeline in \"attractive end markets\" [Actual \u2014 management commentary].\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\nDOV is exposed to:\n- **Rates**: negative correlation with tech/growth longs if rates spike.\n- **Dollar**: if a portfolio already holds large multinational exporters, DOV adds FX overlap.\n- **Recession**: in a stress scenario (2008/2020/2022-type), high-beta industrial correlations converge to ~0.8+. \n- **Conditional VaR estimate**: 2-year tail loss of **\u221215% to \u221220%** from $201.92 in a mild industrial recession; **\u221225% to \u221230%** in a 2008-style credit crisis.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 8. MONITORING & THESIS INTEGRITY\n\n**KPI / Thesis integrity thresholds \u2014 breach triggers re-evaluation**\n\n| KPI | Hold thesis | Re-evaluate at |\n|---|---|---|\n| Organic revenue growth | \u22654% | <2% for two quarters |\n| Book-to-bill | \u22651.0 | <0.95 for two quarters |\n| GAAP operating margin | \u226517% | <15.5% |\n| Adjusted EBITDA margin | \u226525% | <23% |\n| FCF conversion (OCF\u2212capex)/NI | \u226590% | <70% |\n| Net leverage | <2.0x EBITDA | >2.5x |\n| 10Y UST | \u22644.75% | >5.5% sustained |\n\n**Pre-mortem \u2014 3 failure modes**\n\n1. **Demand cliff** \u2014 orders peak in 2026 with book-to-bill 1.06 at the top of the cycle; 2028 revenue \u221210%; early warning: 2 consecutive quarters of book-to-bill <1.0 and organic growth <2%.\n2. **Margin reversal** \u2014 facility consolidation and input-cost inflation outpace pricing; early warning: adjusted EBITDA margin <24% despite revenue growth.\n3. **M&A misallocation** \u2014 management deploys $2B+ into large deals at peak valuation; early warning: acquisitions >50% of market cap in a single year; goodwill step-up >15% of equity.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\n**Step 9-1 Short thesis**\n\n1. DOV is a mature, low-growth conglomerate dressed up as a \"secular growth\" story; only 25% of revenue is secular, the other 75% is industrial cyclicality at late cycle.\n2. Current price embeds 19x+ exit EBITDA; the DCF base case says fair value is $175.\n3. FY2024 reported earnings were inflated by a $2B one-time divestiture gain; investors extrapolating $2.70 EPS from FY2024 are anchoring on a broken number.\n4. Q1 2026 GAAP operating margin was 14.9%; the 17.9% Q2 print reflects timing and mix, not a durable step-change.\n5. PFAS litigation of $235M [Unconfirmed] could compress FCF for years.\n6. SBC is real: $44M/annum and rising; the buyback program partially offsets issuance but shareholder dilution continues.\n7. Strong management commentary may simply reflect the top of a short-cycle recovery; the 2014\u201316 revenue collapse is a legitimate template.\n\n**Step 9-2 Logic combat**\n\n- Long logic strength: **6/10** \u2014 clear execution, margin expansion, strong balance sheet, but valuation is near fair.\n- Short logic strength: **5/10** \u2014 cyclical timing and valuation arguments are real, but the short case depends on a 2027 recession that is not yet visible in orders.\n\nGap = 1 point \u2192 **no conviction downgrade**.\n\n**Step 9-3 Adversarial data**\n\nI found no specific Hindenburg-style short-seller report on DOV [Unconfirmed]. The strongest adversarial/activist angle is regulatory PFAS exposure, which remains unverified from filings.\n\n**Step 9-4 Killed arguments**\n\n- \"DOV is a melting ice-cube conglomerate\" \u2014 killed by 3-year revenue CAGR +1.8%, but 5-yr CAGR 3.9%, and 2026 orders +16% (valid if orders fade).\n- \"DOV is expensive at 25x trailing P/E\" \u2014 valid only if adopting GAAP earnings; on forward adjusted EPS, 18.9x is fair. This argument becomes valid if adjusted EPS misses $10.50.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\n| Audit area | Result |\n|---|---|\n| A. Methodology | Pass \u2014 Engine 1 chosen with explicit rationale; macro, base rate, and scenarios included |\n| B. Valuation | Pass \u2014 DCF, multiples, reverse DCF, and sensitivity presented |\n| C. Bias | Pass with caveat \u2014 DCF output $175 vs consensus target $247; checked for anchoring on guidance |\n| D. Consistency | Pass \u2014 no mixing of GAAP and adjusted EPS |\n| E. Narrative | Pass \u2014 no \"large long-term potential\" unsupported language |\n| F. Red team | Pass \u2014 bear thesis included with same data |\n| G. Data integrity | **Caveat** \u2014 segment data absent, marketable securities not mapped, PFAS unconfirmed, FY2024 tax inputs broken, analyst targets stale. Model confidence: **Moderate**. |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\n- Date: 2026-08-24\n- T0 price: $201.92\n- Base IV: $190.00\n- Current expected value: $191.25\n- MoS: \u22125.6%\n- Key assumptions: 2026 guided revenue 6\u20138%; 2027 +5.1%; 2028\u201330 +4%; op margin to 18.8%; WACC 9.0%; terminal growth 3.0%.\n- Red-team concern: cyclical peak + price near fair.\n- Action rule: buy below $170\u2013175; trim above $235; hold otherwise.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\n**Action: HOLD \u2014 do not initiate a new position at $201.92.**\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Investment action | Hold / Wait for lower entry |\n| Conviction | 10/15 (High on quality, Low on entry) |\n| Target maximum weight | 4% of portfolio |\n| Suggested entry zone | $170\u2013$175 (base-case MoS >8%) |\n| Suggested trim zone | $235+ (bull case fully priced) |\n| Expected 12-mo total return | \u2248 \u22122% to +6% |\n| Key monitoring KPI | Book-to-bill, organic growth, adjusted EBITDA margin |\n| If thesis breaks | Exit on any two: B2B <0.95, organic growth <2%, adjusted EBITDA margin <23% |\n\n**Bottom line:** Dover is an excellent industrial compounder with a narrow widening moat, strong FCF, disciplined capital allocation, and a solid 2026 order book. But at $201.92, the market is already paying for the bull case. The risk/reward is negative: base-case IV is $190, expected value is $191, and the margin of safety is effectively zero. Patience, not enthusiasm, is the correct position here."}, {"sample": 3, "iv": 145.0, "plausible": true, "reasons": [], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "secs": 390, "report": "```text\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 RS2 v2.0 INTEGRATED INVESTMENT ANALYSIS \u2014 DOVER CORPORATION (DOV)\n\u25a0 T0: 2026-08-24  |  Price $201.92  |  Ticker: DOV\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 0 \u2014 ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25cf Enterprise Archetype: B \u2014 Quality Compounder, with Cyclical (C) exposure through short-cycle capital goods. \n  Rationale (3+ reasons):\n  1. Revenue resilience across cycles: $6.04B (FY2016 trough) \u2192 $8.09B (FY2025) = 3.3% CAGR, no collapse in a 12-yr window [Actual \u2014 pack SEC filings].\n  2. Operating margin range only 11.8%\u201317.0% over 12 years; median 14.8% [Actual \u2014 pack arithmetic]. That is compounder-grade stability, not cyclical amplitude.\n  3. Cash conversion: OCF exceeds net income in most years (FY2025 OCF $1.338B vs NI $1.094B) [Actual].\n\u25cf Engine Selected: Engine 1 \u2014 Traditional DCF + Multiples, with cycle-aware normalization.\n\u25cf Why not Engine 2 (Cyclical)? Dover does not exhibit the classic peak\u2013trough margin collapse of a pure cyclical (e.g., semis, energy equipment). Revenue declined at most \u221213% (2015\u201316); margins never went below 11.8%. Using a pure mid-cycle engine would misclassify the franchise.\n\u25cf Transition status: None. 50-80% criteria not met. No evidence of archetype change.\n\u25cf Why not Engine 3/4/5: No hardware-platform monetization layer (D), no option-driven revenue (E), no single regulatory gate (F).\n\u25cf [Unconfirmed] Segment-level margins exist in the FY2025 release (Engineering 17.3%, Clean Energy 17.4%, Imaging 27.7%) [Estimate \u2014 cited in research brief] but the pack holds zero dimensional XBRL facts; the engine selection